LGPL-3.0-or-later packages
--------------------------

The following packages, pulled in transitively by Next.js 16 as optional
runtime image-optimization helpers, are licensed under LGPL-3.0-or-later:

  @img/sharp-*                   (binary distributions of libvips bindings)
  @img/sharp-libvips-*           (libvips system bindings)

Status in Canon:
  - Not invoked at runtime. Canon does not use the Next.js Image component
    or runtime image optimization (next.config.ts sets
    `images.unoptimized: true`), so sharp's image pipeline is never called
    by Canon application code.
  - Optional dependency. Reproducible install without these packages:
        npm install --omit=optional
    The Canon application functions identically without sharp installed.
  - Source code for these packages is publicly available at
    https://github.com/lovell/sharp under the same license terms.

For users distributing Canon (self-host, fork, or modify) under their own
license, the LGPL-3.0-or-later applicability follows from how those
binaries are linked in their distribution. Canon's MIT license applies
only to source files authored in this repository.

